        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-chrysomallon-squamiferum-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-chrysomallon-squamiferum-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Chrysomallon squamiferum (Holocene extant, 0 Ma) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-chrysomallon-squamiferum-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Chrysomallon squamiferum (Holocene extant, 0 Ma)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a TEM measurement of 2.0 nm nuclei",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim a fossil chronospecies before or after 0 Ma",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the copper spots are the animal's visible color",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Copper activator overlay on the sclerite mask in a 12-frame GIF",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Fastest-mode diffusivity calibration, six-point PDE wavelength sweep, equal-diffusion ablation",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Paratype segmentation, KS test, coherency, and circularity",
        "reported_in_source: Iron-sulfide sclerites (Warén 2003); armor mechanics without a Turing equation (Yao 2010)",
        "reported_in_source: Sclerite-less Gigantopelta as the comparative predecessor (Chen 2015; Wong 2025)",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics",
        "transfer_boundary: 2.0 nm is the assigned detail-scale critical wavelength (~2 greigite cells), not a measured pigment stripe.",
        "transfer_boundary: Matrix-confined diffusivities are assumed so that a molecular wavelength can be selected." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Chrysomallon squamiferum (Holocene (Extant))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Ostrakoderma (Mollusca & Echinodermata)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Chrysomallon" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-chrysomallon-squamiferum-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/chrysomallon_squamiferum_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Chrysomallon squamiferum (Holocene extant, 0 Ma); environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Iron-sulfide sclerites (Warén 2003); armor mechanics without a Turing equation (Yao 2010) | Sclerite-less Gigantopelta as the comparative predecessor (Chen 2015; Wong 2025) | Turing 1952 dispersion and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics; reconstructed_in_script: Fastest-mode diffusivity calibration, six-point PDE wavelength sweep, equal-diffusion ablation | Paratype segmentation, KS test, coherency, and circularity | Copper activator overlay on the sclerite mask in a 12-frame GIF; transfer_boundary: 2.0 nm is the assigned detail-scale critical wavelength (~2 greigite cells), not a measured pigment stripe. | Matrix-confined diffusivities are assumed so that a molecular wavelength can be selected.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a TEM measurement of 2.0 nm nuclei | Does not claim the copper spots are the animal's visible color | Does not claim a fossil chronospecies before or after 0 Ma]; other sources: Greigite, the thio-spinel of iron; a new mineral <https://pubs.geoscienceworld.org/msa/ammin/article/49/5-6/543/54000>; phenomenon_size: 2.5 nm (2.5e-09 m, log10=-8.602 m, tier=1_molecular_nm); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 2.5 nm to 883 nm): 2.5 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-vertex-packing, 2.5 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-bioelectric-polarity, 20 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-turing-wavelength, 39 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-clock-wavefront, 88 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-morphogen-condensation, 108 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-elastic-buckling, 123 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-flux-canalization, 172 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-branching-tree" ;
